{"step_index":121,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-04T13:12:47Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-04T18:42:47+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-04T18:42:47+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/renu5/Downloads/find-skill-repo/all%20github%20repos/new%20wave%20of%20skills/youtube-automation-agent-master/README.md`\nTotal Lines: 605\nTotal Bytes: 35605\nShowing lines 1 to 605\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # AgentTube - ECGHuNZSECqTXabaLjkVrTEnguiNZLkKF1qi8oBGpump\n2: \n3: **The open-source AI agent that runs a YouTube channel end to end.**\n4: \n5: Join our telegram community: https://t.co/L4SzbqosOM\n6: \n7: Research topics â†’ write scripts â†’ generate narration and visuals â†’ assemble videos â†’ optimize metadata â†’ review â†’ schedule â†’ publish â†’ learn from analytics and from what your audience says.\n8: \n9: [![CI](https://github.com/darkzOGx/youtube-automation-agent/actions/workflows/ci.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/darkzOGx/youtube-automation-agent/actions/workflows/ci.yml)\n10: [![MIT License](https://img.shields.io/badge/license-MIT-blue.svg)](LICENSE)\n11: [![Node.js 18+](https://img.shields.io/badge/node-18%2B-43853d.svg)](package.json)\n12: \n13: ## What's new on master\n14: \n15: - **v2.10.0 is now on master:** DarkzSEO discoverability audits, controlled growth experiments, and outcome-aware channel operation are available together in the approval-first workflow.\n16: \n17: ## What's new in v2.10.0\n18: \n19: **AgentTube now has a discoverability adapter layer.** v2.10.0 connects the production pipeline to DarkzSEO without merging the projects or weakening human review, then adds the evidence needed to prove what packaging and strategy actually work:\n20: \n21: - **DarkzSEO Discoverability Preflight:** send a canonical content packageâ€”not the private dashboardâ€”through versioned GEO, AIO, AEO, and web-search checks after metadata and provenance are assembled.\n22: - **Reviewable eviden\n<truncated 35038 bytes>\n Built by\n563: \n564: [@darkzOGx](https://github.com/darkzOGx), a solo builder shipping AI automation and developer tools. Find me on [X](https://x.com/darkzOGx) and [laderalabs.io](https://laderalabs.io).\n565: \n566: If Lumen saves you time, a star helps it reach more developers.\n567: \n568: ## Contributing\n569: \n570: See [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) for ground rules (short version: one focused concern per PR, no lockfile churn, lint + tests must pass). For questions and setup help, use [Discussions](https://github.com/darkzOGx/youtube-automation-agent/discussions) â€” Issues is for bugs.\n571: \n572: 1. Fork the repo\n573: 2. Create a feature branch\n574: 3. Make changes and add tests\n575: 4. Submit a PR\n576: \n577: ```bash\n578: git clone <your-fork>\n579: cd youtube-automation-agent\n580: npm install\n581: npm run lint   # must pass â€” CI runs this on every PR\n582: npm test\n583: ```\n584: \n585: ## License\n586: \n587: MIT â€” see [LICENSE](LICENSE).\n588: \n589: ## Acknowledgments\n590: \n591: - [OpenAI](https://openai.com/) â€” GPT-5.6 Sol, GPT Image 2, GPT-4o-mini-tts\n592: - [OpenRouter](https://openrouter.ai/) â€” unified multi-model API\n593: - [Google](https://ai.google.dev/) â€” Gemini 3.7 Flash, Gemini 3.1 Flash Image, Gemini 3.1 Flash TTS\n594: - [Google Cloud](https://console.cloud.google.com/) â€” YouTube Data API\n595: - [Moonshot AI](https://www.moonshot.ai/) â€” Kimi K3\n596: - [Xiaomi](https://mimo.mi.com/) â€” MiMo V2.5 Pro\n597: - [Zhipu AI](https://z.ai/) â€” GLM-5.3\n598: - [ElevenLabs](https://elevenlabs.io/) â€” Eleven v3 TTS\n599: - [Replicate](https://replicate.com/) â€” Wan 2.7 video generation\n600: - [ConstructionBids.ai](https://constructionbids.ai) - AI scans every federal, state & local public works bid and matches you to contracts you'll win.\n601: \n602: ---\n603: \n604: > This tool is for legitimate content creation. Comply with [YouTube's Terms of Service](https://www.youtube.com/t/terms) and Community Guidelines.\n605: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
