{"step_index":135,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-04T17:42:37Z","content":"Priyanshu,\n\nHere is the exact link: **[Google Cloud Console](https://console.cloud.google.com/)**\n\n**How is it free?**\nGoogle gives every account a daily quota of 10,000 free API units. Uploading one video costs 1,600 units. This means you can automatically upload about 6 videos per day for zero cost. You do not even need to enter a credit card to use the free tier.\n\n**Exactly how to get the credentials (Takes 2 minutes):**\n1. Go to that link and log in with your YouTube Google account.\n2. Click **Create Project** at the top. Name it anything (e.g., \"Manhwa Automation\").\n3. Go to the left menu: **APIs & Services** > **Library**.\n4. Search for **YouTube Data API v3** and click **Enable**.\n5. Go to **APIs & Services** > **Credentials**.\n6. Click **+ Create Credentials** > **OAuth client ID**.\n    * *Note: If it asks you to configure the \"OAuth consent screen\" first, just click \"External\", fill in your email, and click Save/Continue until it's done.*\n7. For Application Type, choose **Desktop app**.\n8. Click **Create**, then click the **Download JSON** button.\n\nSave that JSON file to your computer. Once you have it, tell me where you saved it, and I will put it into the automation folder so the agent can start uploading.","thinking":"**Examining the Query**\n\nI'm currently dissecting the user's request. It's focused on acquiring YouTube Data API credentials for video uploads and emphasizes a desire for a free solution. I'm actively working through the constraint checklist, making sure to avoid insincere responses.\n\n\n**Providing the Key Details**\n\nI've got the essentials compiled. Here's a concise breakdown: The Google Cloud Console is the go-to, and yes, it has a free daily quota, enough for a handful of uploads. I'm providing clear steps for API enablement and credential acquisition, avoiding unnecessary elaboration. 